[{:db/id "q-73562/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "6b79828a-05f9-5f82-bf22-79959354a084" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "952962b3-ca0b-5ba7-aaa5-96353c9dbb08" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "7cb6f76d-7eda-51cd-93e3-2214576b89cb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "14b21b86-6f60-53ad-b6b7-0b9885c5201a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "dfa62b31-2447-5a15-a6df-1cd24ab7a9b1" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "9eba4313-70ef-5888-8cd1-b2e596838327" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73562/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer-field/choices ["q-73562/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" "q-73562/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" "q-73562/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" "q-73562/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" "q-73562/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73562" :question/id #uuid "29ae41f9-7bfa-5f0d-93f0-493d5760a182" :question/math-academy-id "q-73562" :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=0$ in the usual way. Given that the system has a unique zero solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- $A$ is not invertible\n- The system $Ax=b$ has no solution for some $2\\times 1$ column vectors $b.$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the third part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the second part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement I is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-73562/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73562"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-36073"] :question/problem "Consider a system of two linear equations in two variables, represented by the matrix equation $Ax=b$ in the usual way. Given that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- $A$ is invertible\n- $det(A)\\ne 0$\n- $Ax=0$ has an infinite number of solutions" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is true by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true by the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement III is false by the third part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statements I and II are true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection/a1d29e710da7fe7aac7b5331af3fed68608d1f3ee2c45397ff8a2bf73effcee4" :answer/id #uuid "4e2491c8-3992-5033-a799-225d97c66391" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  and  III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection/f875651f7f1318c0bb7eec422091a285a478534fed6eb95898ab3cf27eb909ff" :answer/id #uuid "6e261158-2749-58a8-a570-b61fcbae7353" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection/417031c1aacab50ff0a8bf5ae617f8231a5236b4ea5fcc65cd14a93e3c4e7713" :answer/id #uuid "aa7c9b25-12fc-5ac1-805f-8e0c3b86794d" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  and  III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer/id #uuid "4ae7a3d7-f990-5ac5-bbf2-932a489a4383" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8" :answer/id #uuid "921ae110-e4e7-510f-ab59-186a0cb3c973" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I  only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d0892a77-ce44-577c-a9a2-1c997811c395" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-127918/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" :answer-field/choices ["q-127918/selection/a1d29e710da7fe7aac7b5331af3fed68608d1f3ee2c45397ff8a2bf73effcee4" "q-127918/selection/f875651f7f1318c0bb7eec422091a285a478534fed6eb95898ab3cf27eb909ff" "q-127918/selection/417031c1aacab50ff0a8bf5ae617f8231a5236b4ea5fcc65cd14a93e3c4e7713" "q-127918/selection/f8bc450b7f4fe2953896918c1f5c69e16edb279ae4186289918e142ef04a634f" "q-127918/selection/18f1ea50d5b97ea6ddf4ed047cc851740c3854be5650eb9e76df7f5a3d1456f8"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-127918" :question/id #uuid "a109e6d7-dc35-5583-9b59-06b02bed5042" :question/math-academy-id "q-127918" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations given by\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x+2y=-11 \\\\ y+7x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nGiven that the system has exactly one solution, which of the following statements are true?\n\n- The coefficient matrix is not invertible\n- The determinant of the coefficient matrix is not zero\n- The lines $x+2y=-11$ and $y+7x=4$ intersect at infinitely many  points" :question/worked-solution "Recall that given $A=[\\begin{aligned}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22}\\end{aligned}]$, then according to the invertible matrix theorem the following statements are equivalent:    \n\n- $A$ is invertible.\n\n- The system $Ax=b$ has exactly one solution for any $2\\times 1$ column vector $b.$\n\n- The system $Ax=0$ has the unique zero solution.\n\n- The lines ${a}_{11}x+{a}_{12}y={b}_{1}$ and ${a}_{21}x+{a}_{22}y={b}_{2}$ intersect at exactly one point.\n\n- $det(A)\\ne 0.$\n\nAlso, we are told that the second part of the invertible matrix theorem is true. So, all the other parts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem:\n\n- Statement I is false by the first part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\n- Statement II is true. According to the fifth part of the invertible matrix theorem, the determinant cannot be $0.$\n\n- Statement III is false by the fourth part of the invertible matrix theorem.\n\nTherefore, only statement II is true." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-127918/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d49a7b78-bea1-54e5-8232-3fea0d4eb5a3"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-127918"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-31907/selection/1f1f2fe9df6485d5cdc7916416b2f79699d874348406e639d5daec02cb2e57e6" :answer/id #uuid "93e3195d-5707-5394-bfd7-b5bd392e9b3e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31907/selection/5b26512916f768e66a2b0af106e5aa3e2ff7ee012277d9669a26d349c343f77b" :answer/id #uuid "54ca543d-bb77-5ba7-b8ac-2e7eabcbbe01" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31907/selection/df67a18079e3b7b726c109ae1bf07ae161d9f6d37a928c50361c8787d74f7981" :answer/id #uuid "87c96bd7-cc94-5687-8641-a31f7fa6a9c0" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31907/selection/95f63c11f99a5015c1f73558576052145e00c1cfbb1718f78cf554be0ab200f9" :answer/id #uuid "b7250835-daaf-5fbf-9947-00fb66c3ccc8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-31907/selection/6a87b4860f595a380edef797b2cc43b24d4896fc51da713259b980588721456c" :answer/id #uuid "efc2b2e5-7db6-51af-b3b6-1955fca2208f" :answer/type :answer.type/tex